ctive thyroid eye disease. The study consists of two parts, with a maximum duration of approximately 64 weeks.","detailedDescription":"This study is a multicenter, randomized, double-masked, placebo-controlled Phase III clinical study in inactive TED subjects. Approximately 111 eligible subjects will be randomly assigned to the IBI311 group and the placebo group in a 2:1 ratio on Day 1. The study consists of two parts, with a maximum duration of approximately 64 weeks. Part 1 includes a screening period and a double-masked treatment period, lasting for a total of approximately 28 weeks. Part 2 is a follow-up/open treatment period, lasting for up to approximately 36 weeks."},"designModule":{"designInfo":{"allocation":"RANDOMIZED","interventionModel":"PARALLEL","maskingInfo":{"masking":"QUADRUPLE","whoMasked":["PARTICIPANT","CARE_PROVIDER","INVESTIGATOR","OUTCOMES_ASSESSOR"]},"primaryPurpose":"TREATMENT"},"enrollmentInfo":{"count":111,"type":"ESTIMATED"},"phases":["PHASE3"],"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL"},"eligibilityModule":{"eligibilityCriteria":"Inclusion Criteria:

