dy eye","timeFrame":"Weeks 15, 24 and 48"},{"description":"According to the 7-item European Group on Graves' Ophthalmopathy (EUGOGO) amendment, CAS was used to evaluate clinical activity. For each of the following items, one point is given: spontaneous orbital pain, gaze evoked orbital pain, eyelid swelling, eyelid erythema, conjunctival redness, chemosis, and inflammation of caruncle or plica. The sum of these points is the total score, with 0 indicating no clinical activity and 7 indicating the most severe clinical activity.","measure":"Change from baseline in CAS of the study eye","timeFrame":"Weeks 15, 24 and 48"},{"description":"According to the 7-item European Group on Graves' Ophthalmopathy (EUGOGO) amendment, CAS was used to evaluate clinical activity. For each of the following items, one point is given: spontaneous orbital pain, gaze evoked orbital pain, eyelid swelling, eyelid erythema, conjunctival redness, chemosis, and inflammation of caruncle or plica. The sum of these points is the total score, with 0 indicating no clinical activity and 7 indicating the most severe clinical activity.","measure":"Rate of CAS of 0 or 1 in the study eye","timeFrame":"Weeks 15, 24 and 48"},{"description":"The diplopia response rate was defined as the percentage of participants with an improvement in Gorman diplopia score of ≥ 1 grade","measure":"The diplopia response rate","timeFrame":"Weeks 15, 24 and 48"},{"description":"The diplopia resolution rate was defined as the percentage of participants with Gorman diplopia score = 0","measure":"The diplopia resolution rate","timeFrame":"Weeks 15, 24 and 48"},{"description":"Proptosis assessment: protrusion of the eye from the orbital rim as measured using a Hertel exophthalmometer.","measure":"Change from baseline in proptosis of the fellow eye","timeFrame":"Weeks 15, 24 and 48"},{"description":"Change from baseline of the total GO-QoL score, GO-QoL visual functioning subscale and appearance subscale scores.

